    "LockNetworkModeEntryTipsMessage" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The \"Lock Network Mode\" feature is an internal testing tool designed for advanced users to forcibly configure the device’s network mode.\n\nPlease note:\n⚠️ This feature does not guarantee that the desired network mode can be successfully applied. Incorrect configurations may result in issues such as loss of cellular service or other network abnormalities.\nIn some cases, these issues may not occur immediately, but instead appear after a period of time (for example, several hours later or the next day).\n\nIf you experience no service or other network issues, you may try the following steps to recover:\n1. Restart your device\n2. Restore the carrier configuration to the system default via IPCC Management\n3. If the issue persists, restoring the device to factory settings may be required\n\nThis feature will not cause hardware damage to your device. However, any risks arising from its use are the responsibility of the user.\n\nIf you do not accept these risks, or entered this screen by mistake, it is recommended to tap \"Exit\". The app will automatically close this tool and hide its entry point."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "“锁定网络类型”功能为内部测试工具，主要用于帮助专业用户强制设定设备的网络类型。\n\n请注意：\n⚠️该功能不保证一定能够成功设定为您期望的网络类型，且错误的配置可能会导致蜂窝网络出现“无服务”等异常情况。\n在某些情况下，问题可能不会立即出现，而是在一段时间后（例如数小时或次日）才出现无服务或网络异常。\n\n如果出现无服务或网络异常，您可以尝试以下方法进行恢复：\n1. 重新启动设备\n2. 在 IPCC 管理中将运营商配置恢复为系统默认版本\n3. 如仍无法恢复，可能需要将设备恢复至出厂设置\n\n本功能不会对设备硬件造成损坏，但使用过程中产生的风险需由用户自行承担。\n\n如果您无法接受上述风险，或误进入当前界面，建议您点击“退出”，应用程序将自动关闭该工具并隐藏入口。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
